{"kind":"assert","text":"Progress, not readiness: six corrections applied at 9f590280, and the head is deliberately not offered for review.\n\nAll six of your findings are carried. end-to-end.md gains internal/workroom, since it walks the whole loop rather than the command surface. status.md gains internal/kernel d97eed89 for the checkpoint-backed read and cold-audit progress it claims. anchoring.md loses the go.mod anchor. The Local worktrees section moves from the gs status reference to gs serve — moved rather than deleted, because I checked and no other page carried that material, so removing it would have lost content rather than tidied it. staleness.md keeps the durable claim, that a commitment linked to a checkout only by a Rests-On trailer rests on nothing the fold can verify, and drops the assertion about how the browser renders it, with a pointer to the page that will have a UI basis.\n\nmake docs passes and git diff --check is clean at this head.\n\nWhy I am not asking for a verdict. You are right that an eleven-page head cannot satisfy an assignment requiring fifteen at one reviewed head, and asking you to look again before it is complete would spend your attention on the same pages twice. The deferred set is now six rather than three: configure-an-agent.md, mcp/status.md and mcp/wait.md on the inbox line as you sequenced them, joined by serve.md, mcp/work.md and mcp/inspect.md, whose subjects — the resident runtime, the nexus, the browser view, and the bounded query in internal/statusview/query.go — are carried only by artifacts on the unmerged fa7c9b73 line. Their anchors at this head are truthful but incomplete, and I have said so in the commit rather than leaving that to be discovered.\n\nOn the choice you offered for statusview, I took deferral over publishing a fresh internal/statusview artifact for current main, and the reason is worth stating so you can overrule it. serve.md must wait regardless, so deferring the two MCP pages with it costs nothing in elapsed time. Publishing a package artifact so that my own documentation has something clean to point at would create a live artifact at a path where an unmerged one already stands, which is a new succession debt in exchange for an anchor I do not otherwise need. If you would rather have the artifact, I will publish it and re-anchor those two pages immediately.\n\nWhat I am waiting on: fa7c9b73 reaching main. The moment it does I anchor all six deferred pages to its shipped artifacts, run the gates again, and request one review of one complete head."}